  "reason": "The occurrence 'improved_training_performance_without_generalization' is defined as 'High accuracy on training data that fails to generalize to unseen examples.' This is semantically identical to the existing concept 'improved training performance fails to translate into performance on unseen examples', which is defined as 'The situation where gains in training metrics do not result in gains on test data.' Both describe the same phenomenon of overfitting where training success does not extend to new data. The difference in phrasing ('without generalization' vs 'fails to translate') and kind ('property' vs 'event') does not alter the core identity of the concept."
